事实上，在资助噪音研究方面，欧洲绝对领先于我们。相机的工作原理就像测速相机一样。当一辆改装了消音器的汽车呼啸着开过街角时，就会拍下一张车牌的照片，并记录下声级。早期的问题之一是，如果你旁边有一辆车，那可能会增加到声级中，所以发出巨响的不是你的车。而是你旁边那辆车的贡献。所以他们必须解决这个问题。

46
00:32:47.000 --> 00:33:28.000
And so New York City now is a pilot study, and they have found that when people are penalized, that there's less noise in the area, but they only have a few cameras. They haven't yet issued a full report on it, but it's a way of trying to get people to recognize that they cannot make noise on the road, just as there are rules by which your cars are guided with respect to speed. There are rules with respect to noise. So this is being explored and people are interested in it. One last question.
因此，纽约市现在正在进行试点研究，他们发现当人们受到惩罚时，该地区的噪音就会减少，但他们只有几台相机。他们还没有发布关于它的完整报告，但这是一种试图让人们认识到他们不能在路上制造噪音的方法，就像有关于你的汽车行驶速度的规则一样。有关于噪音的规则。所以这正在被探索，人们对此很感兴趣。最后一个问题。

47
00:33:28.000 --> 00:34:06.000
I want to ask you, what are the strangest noise complaints that you've gotten? Can you just hit me with one or two of those? Okay. A woman called me, an older woman, and said a car was parked in front of her apart in building, small building, blasting music late at night. and then she would hear footsteps going upstairs and downstairs, and she couldn't sleep. I said, what's going on? So her aide got on the phone, said Dr. Bronset, they're dealing drugs above.
我想问你，你接到的最奇怪的噪音投诉是什么？你能给我说一两个那样的例子吗？好的。一个女人打电话给我，一个老妇人，说一辆车停在她公寓大楼前，一个小建筑，深夜放着震耳欲聋的音乐，然后她会听到楼上楼下的脚步声，她睡不着觉。我说，怎么回事？于是她的助手接起电话说，布朗萨夫博士，他们在楼上毒品交易。

48
00:34:06.000 --> 00:34:50.000
And I must say, I went to the precinct of that Brooklyn community, spoke to them, and they said, we'll look into it. They did. The drug dealing was shut down. down. The next call I got was from the landlord who had been so frightened he couldn't do anything about it, thanking me profusely and said I will do everything for that person. Now I'm going to give you another one. I get a complaint that the person next door to this other couple are hearing the bed banging against the wall at night when the couple has sex.
我必须说，我去了那个布鲁克林社区的警察局，跟他们谈了谈，他们说，我们会调查的。他们照做了。毒品交易被查封了。我接到的下一个电话是房东打来的，他吓坏了，对此束手无策，他对我千恩万谢，并说我将为那个人做一切事情。现在我再给你讲一个。我接到一个投诉，说这另一对夫妇隔壁的人晚上听到床撞击墙壁的声音，当这对夫妇做爱时。

49
00:34:50.000 --> 00:35:57.000
that's a touchy one. Fortunately, it was in my building, and I knew the housekeeper of that apartment. And I approached, I said, you know, the people next door are saying the bed bangs against the wall. So I would suggest you move the bed a few inches away from the wall, and that's how that problem was solved. And then I'll give you my one early case. A man decided to build a windmill in his back. I actually went out to New Jersey and listened to that windmill. And I can tell you, even when I walked into her home, it was still in my head. The good news, the windmill was taken down. And from what I hear, that case is discussed in law classes. So sex, drug dealing, windmills, I don't think you can come up with something that I haven't yet. Well, I want to thank you for joining me today and thank you for making the world a little bit less noisy.
这是一个敏感的话题。幸好它就在我的大楼里，我认识那个公寓的管家。我走过去说，你知道，隔壁的人说床撞击了墙壁。所以我建议你把床往外挪几英寸，问题就是这样解决的。然后我给你讲我早期的一个案子。一个男人决定在后院建一个风车。我实际上去了新泽西州听了那个风车。我可以告诉你，即使我走进她的家，它依然在我的脑海里回响。好消息是，风车被拆除了。据我所听到的，这个案子在法学课上被讨论过。所以性、毒品交易、风车，我想你不可能想出什么我还不知道的东西。好吧，我想感谢你今天加入我，也感谢你让世界变得不那么嘈杂一点。

